### Why a command typed beside a running node cannot be handed to it. Each is said
### after "is running here, and".

typed-kept-meet = it looks for nodes only where it always does.
    Leave --meet out, or run this when it has stopped.
typed-kept-pack = a node is packed only while it is not running. Nothing was
    written. `333 stop`, then pack it.
typed-kept-moved = where a node lives is recorded only while it is not running.
    `333 stop`, then run this again.
typed-kept-languages = it reads the catalogs, not the running node.
typed-kept-service = it asks the service manager, not the running node.

typed-kept-invite = it reads what this node wrote, and asks the running node nothing.
